      "intel_summary": "All 5 queried source IPs (203.0.113.17, 203.0.113.24, 203.0.113.59, 203.0.113.23, and 203.0.113.21) were identified as 'malicious' under the botnet category. Intelligence notes indicate they match the 203.0.113.0/24 subnet and are actively associated with distributed credential-stuffing botnet activity.",
      "enrichment_notes": "Threat intelligence confirms that the queried IPs belong to a known distributed credential-stuffing botnet operating out of the 203.0.113.0/24 range. This strongly reinforces that the observed high-frequency burst (40 login attempts across 26 distinct IPs in 2.68 seconds targeting accounts like admin, alice, root, and guest) is a coordinated automated credential-stuffing/brute-force campaign rather than organic user traffic. Most critically, the presence of 2 successful logins alongside 38 failures indicates potential account compromise, significantly elevating the incident's severity and necessitating immediate investigation and remediation for the compromised accounts.",
